{"format":1,"seq":123,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to map git method names to actual CLI subcommands, like revParse to rev-parse and lsRemote to ls-remote, since the command source uses the method directly as the args. I'll add that lookup and make sure the header display also shows the correct hyphenated subcommand name.\n\nThen there's the workspace.edit type issue -- the changes array type rejects arrays produced by .map, and the anchor type rejects plain strings, so I should widen both types while keeping runtime validation intact, and update the batch docs to clarify the edit shape. I also need to check how edit-spec.ts validates anchors and non-empty changes before finalizing the widened types.\n\nFinally, I should look into where sandbox globals like atob/btoa are declared so I can add their type definitions alongside the other guest globals.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01FJVGvn6byAQjvTj56QhjyM","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read edit-spec and find sandbox lib declarations\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read, search } }) => {\n  const [es, lib] = await Promise.all([\n    read(\"src/workspace/edit-spec.ts\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    search(\"declare (function|var|const) (console|setTimeout|structuredClone|TextEncoder)|lib: \\\\[|\\\"lib\\\\.|lib\\\\.es\", { path: \"src\", regex: true, limit: 30, contextLines: 1 }),\n  ]);\n  return { es: es.content, lib: lib.matches?.map((m: any) => `${m.file}:${m.line}: ${m.text}`) };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":909,"cacheRead":54435,"cacheWrite":1166,"totalTokens":56512,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":628},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794681531711,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_jgv5